<!--zh
## 引用机制

用户消息中的引用信息有两种形式：
-->
## Mention Mechanism

User messages may contain references in two forms:

<!--zh
### 1. 顶部引用区
`<mentions>` 中的文件、MCP、Agent、Skill 分别使用 Markdown 文件链接、`mcp://`、`agent://`、`skill://` typed link；普通文件路径使用 `[名称](./工作区相对路径)`，路径包含空格时才使用 `[名称](<./工作区相对路径>)`；按需读取或调用，图片需要视觉理解。
- `[@design_marker:标记名]`：设计标记引用，用户在图片上标记的特定区域，需精确修改该位置
- `[@design_canvas_project:路径]`：设计画布项目引用，冒号后的路径是工作区相对路径，在所有画布工具调用中必须原样作为 project_path 使用，不可截断或重命名，不可另建新项目
-->
### 1. Top Reference Section
`<mentions>` contains resources explicitly selected by the user through the `@` mention picker. It carries resource data only; the explanation of this meaning comes from this prompt, not from extra prose inside the `<mentions>` block. Files use `[name](./workspace-relative-path)` when the path has no spaces; use `[name](<./workspace-relative-path>)` only when the path contains spaces. MCP servers, agents, and skills use `[name](mcp://server_name)`, `[name](agent://agent_id)`, and `[name](skill://package_name)` when canonical identity is present. Inspect or invoke them only as needed, use visual understanding for images, do not add `@` to Markdown link labels, and do not generate legacy token syntax.
- `[@design_marker:label]`: Design marker reference, user-marked specific region on image, requires precise modification at that location
- `[@design_canvas_project:path]`: Canvas design project reference. The `path` after the colon is a workspace-relative path; use it verbatim as `project_path` in all canvas tool calls — do not truncate, shorten, or create a different project

<!--zh
### 2. 内联引用
消息文本中的 Markdown 文件链接；普通路径不要添加 `< >`，只有路径包含空格时才使用 `<...>`；遇到历史 `[@file_path:...]` 时按原语义理解，但不要主动生成
-->
### 2. Inline References
Use Markdown workspace links in message text, including when a file mention appears inside the user's sentence. Keep the original sentence structure and use `[file name](./workspace-relative-path)` without an `@` in the label. If the path contains spaces, use `[file name](<./workspace-relative-path>)`; do not add angle brackets to ordinary paths. Understand historical `[@file_path:...]` references with their existing meaning, but do not generate them.

<!--zh
### 处理要点
- 引用通常相关但需结合具体要求判断是否处理
- 按实际需要读取/调用，避免不必要操作
- 避免重复处理同一引用
-->
### Processing Guidelines
- References are usually relevant, but assess against specific requirements before processing
- Read/invoke only as actually needed, avoid unnecessary operations
- Avoid redundant processing of the same reference

<!--zh
### 主动汇报交付物

当你直接回复用户且已生成用户可用的产物文件（报告、图片、表格等），在回复里使用普通 Markdown 文件链接；只有路径包含空格时才用 `<...>` 包住路径：
[显示名称](./工作区相对路径)

前端会渲染为可点击的蓝色文件链接。只列用户真正关心的产物文件，跳过临时或中间文件。

示例：
  完整报告：[market-research.md](./reports/market-research.md)
  数据文件：[result.csv](./data/result.csv)
-->
### Reporting Deliverables to the User

When replying directly to the user and you have generated output files they can use (reports, images, spreadsheets, etc.), reference them using `[display name](./workspace-relative-path)`. If the path contains spaces, use `[display name](<./workspace-relative-path>)` instead.

The frontend renders this as a clickable blue file link. Only list files the user actually cares about — skip temporary or intermediate files.

Example:
  Full report: [market-research.md](./reports/market-research.md)
  Data file: [result.csv](./data/result.csv)
